  "_comment": [
    "Prompting acceptance tolerances (vocabulary / context prompt / INSTRUCT / transcript prefix).",
    "",
    "C++ outputs are compared against the reference implementations' outputs on the same data:",
    "earnings22 chunked, 283 utts (instruct: first 20), greedy decoding. Harness and reference",
    "results: ~/sandboxes/transcribe/tmp/prompt-ab (README.md, results*/); design and measured",
    "reference behavior: notes/prompting-api-proposal-v2.md, notes/prompting-ab-results.md.",
    "",
    "Gates, per model and condition, as |C++ - reference|:",
    "  wer_abs        corpus WER (EnglishTextNormalizer), absolute points",
    "  recall_pts     dictionary-term recall, points",
    "  follow_pts     INSTRUCT follow-rate, points",
    "  cont_wer_abs   prefix continuation WER, absolute points",
    "  dup_pts        prefix duplication rate, points",
    "plus rendered-prompt parity: the decoded decoder/LLM input must equal the reference's",
    "(audio placeholder runs collapsed) on every row the reference records.",
    "",
    "Proposed from the first C++ acceptance run (2026-09-27, branch generic-prompting). Several",
    "C++ runs used Q8_0 against a BF16/F32 reference (noted per model), so the gates carry",
    "quantization noise; the observed deltas below are well inside them except where noted.",
    "Known excursions that are not prompting defects:",
    "  - A single looping utterance dominates corpus WER when the two harnesses stop it at",
    "    different lengths (reference max_new_tokens=128, C++ repetition guard / 256-token",
    "    budget). whisper-large-v3 ctx_prev (+1.13) and canary-1b-v2 prefix (-2.59) both",
    "    fall inside the gate once that one or two utterances are excluded (11.8 vs 11.7;",
    "    11.99 vs 11.84). Compare with those excluded, or cap C++ generation to match.",
    "  - granite-4.1-2b-plus kw: C++ WER 1.11 better than the reference on Q8_0 with identical",
    "    term hits; treat improvements beyond the gate as noise, not a failure."
  ],
